# GitHub Connect → Create Repo → Push Code

## GitHub account

- Profile: https://github.com/omgupta210
- Owner: `omgupta210`
- Default remote: `https://github.com/omgupta210/<repo-name>.git`

## Prerequisites (Windows)

Git and GitHub CLI may not be in PATH. Use full paths:

```bat
set GIT=C:\Program Files\Git\cmd\git.exe
set GH=C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe
```

Verify:

```bat
"%GIT%" --version
"%GH%" --version
"%GH%" auth status
```

If Git missing → https://git-scm.com/download/win  
If `gh` missing → https://cli.github.com/  
If not logged in → run `"%GH%" auth login` (browser login required; cannot skip)

## Workflow checklist

```text
- [ ] Confirm project folder path
- [ ] Confirm repo name (kebab-case or snake_case, e.g. config_server_code)
- [ ] Ensure .gitignore exists (target/, .metadata/, .env, secrets)
- [ ] Login: gh auth login
- [ ] Create repo on GitHub
- [ ] git init → add → commit → push to main
- [ ] Return repo URL to user
```

## Step 1 — Connect to GitHub

```bat
"%GH%" auth login -h github.com -p https -w
"%GH%" auth status
```

Must show: `Logged in to github.com as omgupta210` (or correct username).

Alternative: set `GH_TOKEN` with a Personal Access Token from https://github.com/settings/tokens

## Step 2 — Prepare local project

From project root (e.g. `D:\spring_server_code`):

**Required `.gitignore` for Java/Maven:**

```gitignore
target/
.metadata/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
.idea/
*.iml
.env
```

**Commit without changing global git config** (use inline identity):

```bat
cd D:\spring_server_code
"%GIT%" init
"%GIT%" add .
"%GIT%" -c user.name="omgupta210" -c user.email="omgupta210@users.noreply.github.com" commit -m "Initial commit: <description>"
"%GIT%" branch -M main
```

## Step 3 — Create repo on GitHub

**Preferred (GitHub CLI):**

```bat
cd D:\spring_server_code
"%GH%" repo create omgupta210/<repo-name> --public --description "<short description>" --source=. --remote=origin --push
```

Examples:

```bat
"%GH%" repo create omgupta210/config_server_code --public --description "Spring Boot Config Server + Hello World" --source=. --remote=origin --push
```

**If repo already exists locally with remote:**

```bat
"%GIT%" remote remove origin
"%GIT%" remote add origin https://github.com/omgupta210/<repo-name>.git
"%GIT%" push -u origin main
```

**If repo created manually on https://github.com/new:**

- Name: `<repo-name>`
- Do NOT add README if local README exists
- Then push only (Step 4)

## Step 4 — Push code

```bat
cd D:\spring_server_code
"%GIT%" push -u origin main
```

On auth prompt: use GitHub username + Personal Access Token (not password).

## Step 5 — Verify

```bat
"%GH%" repo view omgupta210/<repo-name> --web
```

Confirm URL loads: `https://github.com/omgupta210/<repo-name>`

## Project shortcut script

If `push-to-github.bat` exists in project root, run it:

```bat
cd D:\spring_server_code
push-to-github.bat
```

It handles login check, repo create, and push for `config_server_code`.

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| Repo not visible on profile | Never pushed / repo not created | Complete Step 1–4; local commit alone is not enough |
| `Repository not found` | Repo doesn't exist on GitHub | Create with `gh repo create` first |
| `git not recognized` | Not in PATH | Use `C:\Program Files\Git\cmd\git.exe` |
| `gh auth login` required | Not logged in | Run auth login in terminal (interactive) |
| `Author identity unknown` | No git user config | Use `-c user.name=... -c user.email=...` on commit |
| Push rejected / 403 | Bad credentials | Regenerate PAT at github.com/settings/tokens |

## Safety rules

- Never commit `.env`, passwords, API keys, or tokens
- Never run `git push --force` to `main` unless user explicitly asks
- Never update global `git config`
- Only commit when user asks to deploy or push
- Never skip hooks unless user requests

